aler's polling lead further.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": []}, "overview": "The new 9th District, drawn to favor Republicans by roughly nine points, features an open-seat contest between Trump-backed Republican Alex Mealer and Democrat Leticia Gutierrez. Mealer holds a heavy financial advantage, having raised about $2.7 million and drawn nearly $5 million in outside support, while Gutierrez has raised roughly $55,000. Raters across the spectrum place the race in the Likely R column, with one calling it Solid R and another Safe R.\n\nPolling shows a consistent but modest Republican lead: a University of Houston survey in early October had Mealer ahead 48-42 among likely voters, matching a September PPP result of 45-39. Prediction markets give Gutierrez roughly a one-in-six chance. Headlines note Trump's struggles and Mealer's efforts to distance herself from him, suggesting some Democratic upside in a favorable national environment, but the district's fundamentals and the resource gap favor Mealer heading into November.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0912, "margin": -8.44}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0891, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0766, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1178, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0737, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0642, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0775, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0899, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0901, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0919, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1301, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1157, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1517, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0916, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0727, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0914, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_de